# =========================
# BedrockSentry .gitignore
# =========================

## .NET build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
out/
publish/
*.pdb

## Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## NuGet
*.nupkg
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

## Test results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Logs
*.log
logs/

## Local configuration and secrets — never commit real config
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
**/config.local.*
*.env

## Local-only working files: results, scratchpads and hand-created toggles.
## These two rules exist because nothing enforced the convention before them —
## such files had simply never been committed, which is not the same as being
## safe from it.
*.local
*.local.md

## The rest of the working state left behind by running this software on a real
## machine. These were ignored only by .git/info/exclude, which is machine-local,
## uncommitted and survives no clone — so a fresh checkout shows live worlds and
## player data as untracked, and the "git status is clean afterwards" safety
## signal drowns in them.
/test-instances/
/.claude/test-mode.json
/.claude/settings.local.json

## TLS certificates — generated at runtime, never committed
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

## Runtime data: BDS installs, worlds, backups, player database.
## Scoped to specific runtime roots rather than matching folder names
## anywhere, so nothing under companion-pack/ or src/ is ever caught by
## accident. The BDS binary itself is downloaded per-install and must never be
## committed: Minecraft's usage guidelines require every copy to come from Mojang.
/instances/
/bedrock-server/
/bds/
/backups/
worlds/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
players.json
config-export*.json

## Zips, in both directions. package-local.ps1 writes its release archive to the
## repository root by default — a ~120 MB self-contained publish, which is build
## output however it is named — and a Bedrock download landing here must never be
## committed at all. The rules above only cover those as
## directories, so a zip sitting beside them would otherwise be staged by a plain
## `git add .`.
bedrocksentry-*.zip
bedrock-server-*.zip

## OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Misc
*.tmp
*.bak
node_modules/
